[agent] The deliverable is complete and verified. The feature table `featureseb4964` version 1 exists on the Hopsworks platform with all 700 rows readable through both the offline store (Feature Query Service) and the online store.
[agent] **What was built:** an online-enabled feature group `featureseb4964` v1 in project `mlpabe9908d`'s feature store, with primary key `row_id`, event-time column `event_time` (kept as bigint epoch milliseconds), and exactly the columns `row_id, account_id, event_time, amount_usd, is_weekend, amount_7d`.
[agent] **How it ran (all platform-side):** I uploaded `transactions.csv` and `fx_rates.csv` plus a job script to the project's dataset storage, then created and ran a Hopsworks Python job (`featureseb4964_build`, environment `python-feature-pipeline`) on the cluster. The job reads the CSVs from the `/hopsfs` mount, joins on currency for `amount_usd = amount × fx_rate`, computes `is_weekend` from the UTC day-of-week, and computes `amount_7d` per account as the sum of `amount` over the inclusive window `[event_time − 7 days, event_time]` (via sorted per-account prefix sums with two-sided-inclusive boundaries), then `get_or_create_feature_group(..., online_enabled=True)` and `insert(..., wait=True)`.
[agent] **Verification:** a second platform job read the group back — offline read returned 700 rows and online read returned 700 rows with identical values; spot check confirms correctness (e.g. R00000: 25.22 GBP × 1.27 = 32.0294, weekend flag set, and the earliest rows' 7-day sum equals their own amount).
[agent] Notable environment friction I had to work around (all within the allowed interface): the sandbox only permits localhost traffic, and `NO_PROXY` contained `10.0.0.0/8`, which made the SDK bypass the local proxy — overriding `NO_PROXY` fixed connectivity; one dataset upload reported success but didn't persist and needed a re-upload; and local Arrow Flight reads are impossible because gRPC won't route through the HTTP proxy, which is why verification ran as a cluster job.
